s are travelling around</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice and useful as well. Thanks for sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T08:23:39-07:00","id":723124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/722210-ex-3-i-scaled-up-the-world-map?p=723064#post723064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good job. I also find this one very useful, as it has a 500 mile squared grid so is useful for working out distances if your characters are travelling around:</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, awesome, thanks. I missed that from 2nd edition. I ran that one through Waifu as well.<br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/MlgV37u.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Here it is, 5780x3740px with grid. </a>I'll update the OP as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8825-nallenon","name":"Nallenon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T09:53:10-08:00","id":766329,"title":"","content":"Have you found a place to host the 11560x7480px variation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/660-souls512","name":"Souls512","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar660_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T09:58:36-08:00","id":766340,"title":"","content":"Very nice, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T02:55:06-08:00","id":772178,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much for this! I had it printed in poster size 24x36 inches, Holy hell its beautiful, didnt pixilate or blur at all, and looks sharp and crisp. It looks beautiful above my desk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was concerned it would blur at that size, and for 15 bucks it was a gamble but damn i wanted this map on my wall now to impatient to wait for my cloth map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:56:45-08:00","id":772505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/722210-ex-3-i-scaled-up-the-world-map?p=723064#post723064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good job. I also find this one very useful, as it has a 500 mile squared grid so is useful for working out distances if your characters are travelling around:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/5kT5zWB.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">http://i.imgur.com/5kT5zWB.jpg</span></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at that map and the scale provided, those squares actually look a bit smaller than 500 miles across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:25:51-08:00","id":772660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/722210-ex-3-i-scaled-up-the-world-map?p=772505#post772505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking at that map and the scale provided, those squares actually look a bit smaller than 500 miles across.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are actually pretty much pixel-perfect to the scale listed from center of grid-line to center of grid-line, I just checked in Photoshop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T21:30:43-08:00","id":772792,"title":"","content":"A thousand thank yous! It looks great and I can actually read it now. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T23:17:52-07:00","id":885979,"title":"","content":"Just found this 'scaled' map and it helps me greatly, thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Long time lurker","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8781-happy-hermit","name":"Happy Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8781_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T01:40:05-07:00","id":886028,"title":"","content":"I should say, I didn't make this map, someone else did.<br /> But I don't remember who... but that guy/girl should get credit for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T06:22:56-07:00","id":932878,"title":"","content":"Thanks for uploading that map. Together with a bit research about the fonts and some playing with layers in gimp, I can start to mod the world map with the Kingdoms of my group!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/oKAqjP1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Turns into <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/8jFfsd2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Walkthrough:<br /> <br /> 1) open map<br /> 2) copy the map layer, call it &quot;<b>shadow layer</b>&quot;<br /> 2.1) Change the contrast up and the saturation till you find it to be some extra dirty look (less contrast, less saturation)<br /> 2.2) Declare white to be transparent, thus dimming it out some<br /> 2.3) Add a <u>layer mask</u> of full transparecy (full black!) - we will come back to the layer later<br /> 3) copy the icons you want to place on the map from the back layer<br /> 3.1) insert them onto a new, fully transparent layer under the shadow layer. Position them carefully<br /> 3.2) add lines (for example the traderoutes) and edit them to your liking.<br /> 4) add the captions on a layer just below the shadow layer, it is the <b>text layer</b><br /> 4.1) Font is Boister Black, as said <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880178-exalted-3-fonts\">here</a><br /> 4.2) I like to use a reddish color (H11 S87 V27 R70 G20 B9 or: #461409)<br /> 5) copy the text layer, place it under the text layer, call it &quot;<b>text backdrop</b>&quot;<br /> 5.1) paint the text white, use a blur filter<br /> 5.2) repeat 5.1) twice.<br /> 6) select the very edges of the text on the <i>text layer</i><br /> 6.1) edit the <u>layer mask</u> of the <i>shadow layer</i><br /> 6.2) fill in the selection with pure white<br /> 6.3) apply 2 to 3 times the blur filter, until the dirt blends with the shadow nicely<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T13:01:18-07:00","id":1237561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/722210-ex-3-i-scaled-up-the-world-map?p=932878#post932878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for uploading that map. Together with a bit research about the fonts and some playing with layers in gimp, I can start to mod the world map with the Kingdoms of my group!<br /> <br /> Walkthrough:<br /> <br /> 1) open map<br /> 2) copy the map layer, call it &quot;<b>shadow layer</b>&quot;<br /> 2.1) Change the contrast up and the saturation till you find it to be some extra dirty look (less contrast, less saturation)<br /> 2.2) Declare white to be transparent, thus dimming it out some<br /> 2.3) Add a <u>layer mask</u> of full transparecy (full black!) - we will come back to the layer later<br /> 3) copy the icons you want to place on the map from the back layer<br /> 3.1) insert them onto a new, fully transparent layer under the shadow layer. Position them carefully<br /> 3.2) add lines (for example the traderoutes) and edit them to your liking.<br /> 4) add the captions on a layer just below the shadow layer, it is the <b>text layer</b><br /> 4.1) Font is Boister Black, as said <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880178-exalted-3-fonts\">here</a><br /> 4.2) I like to use a reddish color (H11 S87 V27 R70 G20 B9 or: #461409)<br /> 5) copy the text layer, place it under the text layer, call it &quot;<b>text backdrop</b>&quot;<br /> 5.1) paint the text white, use a blur filter<br /> 5.2) repeat 5.1) twice.<br /> 6) select the very edges of the text on the <i>text layer</i><br /> 6.1) edit the <u>layer mask</u> of the <i>shadow layer</i><br /> 6.2) fill in the selection with pure white<br /> 6.3) apply 2 to 3 times the blur filter, until the dirt blends with the shadow nicely</div> </div> </div> </div>It's never late to thank someone for their help =) <br /> Thank you Hira Akigi for these tips!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you like Alchemicals, please check out my DeviantArt Gallery!! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> - 5 Magic Materials BeamKlaves and Gyroscopic Chakrans ? OK<br /> - Autochthonia updated World Map? OK<br /> And many more! <a href=\"http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals\" target=\"_blank\">http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2498-yukiartic","name":"Yukiartic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T15:52:27-07:00","id":1238083,"title":"","content":"So, out of curiosity, I decided to do a sketch of what the world map would look like if it only did an Exalted-style sketch with major cities. I decided to use Wikipedia's list of cities by population, and (after skipping over a few major Chinese cities because geez there are a lot of big Chinese cities), you end up with something like this: <div align=\"center\"> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/cu5zOSq.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> If you go by cities proper, mainland Europe doesn't even have one in the top fifty! If you go by general urban areas then Paris ends up in the thirties, but cities proper puts Madrid in the seventies.<br /> <br /> I think its fair to say that the Exalted map is probably showing us the major cities of Creation. But, I mean, Jesus, the amount of blank area on the Creation map is ridiculous! There are some patches where you can fit nearly the entire continent of Europe into the blank spaces.<br /> <br /> It's probably a really mundane thing to notice, but it caught my attention. By combining a cities-centric map with the sheer size of Creation, the map of Creation leaves us with a <b>lot</b> of free space. That should comfort me by saying it's easy to fit in whatever I need wherever I need it, but instead I'm just kind of intimidated by the scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24333-electronsutra","name":"ElectronSutra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24333_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}